From c2c4b757c572fe9b19952a385a7c600b8a5f6b52 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Bla=C5=BE=20Zupan?= <blaz@inlimbo.org>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 09:22:52 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: brcmfmac: keep ARP and ND offload off on the BCM4355
 too
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Apple firmware for the BCM4355 (MacBookAir8,1/8,2, firmware
9.30.503.0.32.5.87) has the same ND offload problem as the BCM4364.
With ARP/ND offload enabled, the firmware console logs
"EL: 38 5890 0 d8ac0 ffffffff" several times per second. After a
while the association degrades: downloads are capped at ~48 Mbit/s
aggregate even with parallel streams, ping to the LAN gateway rises
from 4 ms to ~120 ms under load (the AP queues frames the client does
not take), and uploads are unaffected. Reconnecting clears it until
the next time.

With the offloads off (interface promiscuous), the firmware errors
stop and downloads stay at 300-400 Mbit/s.

Extend the BCM4364 check to the BCM4355.

Signed-off-by: Blaž Zupan <blaz@inlimbo.org>
---
 .../net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c    | 10 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c
index 6eae713..8a9c342 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c
@@ -105,11 +105,13 @@ void brcmf_configure_arp_nd_offload(struct brcmf_if *ifp, bool enable)
 	}
 
 	/* With ND offload on while awake, the Apple firmware for the BCM4364
-	 * makes IPv6 downloads drop to low rates. macOS runs ARP and ND
-	 * offload only in sleep, keep both off on this chip.
+	 * and BCM4355 makes downloads drop to low rates. macOS runs ARP and
+	 * ND offload only in sleep, keep both off on these chips.
 	 */
-	if (enable && ifp->drvr->bus_if->chip == BRCM_CC_4364_CHIP_ID) {
-		brcmf_dbg(TRACE, "Skip ARP/ND offload enable on BCM4364\n");
+	if (enable && (ifp->drvr->bus_if->chip == BRCM_CC_4364_CHIP_ID ||
+		       ifp->drvr->bus_if->chip == BRCM_CC_4355_CHIP_ID)) {
+		brcmf_dbg(TRACE, "Skip ARP/ND offload enable on BCM%x\n",
+			  ifp->drvr->bus_if->chip);
 		enable = false;
 	}
 
